    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d168">

                <pb facs="0242" n="228" sameAs="frus:frus1949v07p1/pg228"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BC Indonesia/2–1449: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Consulate General at Batavia
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d168-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret   us urgent</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                        
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-02-14T18:00:00-05:00">February 14,
                            1949—6 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>82. Usgoc 291. Neth <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >aide-mémoire</hi><anchor n="2" xml:id="d168-f2"/> reed today urges
                    postponement UNCFI Report re establishment
                    interim govt to reasonable later date due to Dutch cabinet crisis and delay
                    Cochran’s arrival Batavia. Dept considers
                    request reasonable and trusts report can be delayed for brief period. Your
                    comments desired.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d168-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d168-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated as 118 to The Hague and as 78 to New York (USUN).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d168-f2" n="2" xml:id="d168-f2-content">
